!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Cross-section data for Cl2O2 + hv --> Cl + ClOO
! source : JPL-2011 (note F7 and table 4F-11)
!
! Rem1: Values changed in JPL-2011 over JPL-2006==JPL-2002. Summary from note F7:
!       - These changes are VERY IMPORTANT for (polar) ozone depletion especially at wl>300 nm.
!       - Temperature dependence is very weak if any
!       - for atmospheric studies, Cl2O2 *is* ClOOCl
!       - other branch -> ClO+ClO has much smaller q.y. (if any) and is neglected here
!
! Rem2: as recommended by JPL-2011 note F7, the values are extended for wl>420nm by 
!       crs = 9.5e-16*exp(-0.0281*wl) (crs in cm2, wl in nm)
!       Here this extrapolation is done until 570nm where crs reaches 1e-22 cm2
!
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        60  | Finishes at wl interval :  146
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
